      ['Headroom: the question-number head’s seen balanced accuracy must lie above chance + 5 pp and below 95%. It passed on all three primary blocks; the levels are in the tables above.'],
      ['Triviality canary: a ridge classifier on per-channel mean and log-variance must not answer the seen task by itself. It passed on BETA (on the first fold’s ', n(triv.BETA.training_people!), ' training people) and on BOAS and EESM19 (carried from route 2); none is declared for motor imagery, so its gate reads “not run”.'],
      ['Read-off floor: an unseen sleep cell counts only if the read-off’s AUROC interval lies above 0.55. ', n(G.readoff_floor.primary_cells_passing), ' of ', n(G.readoff_floor.primary_cells), ' primary and ', n(G.readoff_floor.secondary_cells_passing), ' of ', n(G.readoff_floor.secondary_cells), ' secondary cells passed.'],
      ['Shuffled-EEG scorer check: each primary aggregate, recomputed with the test features shuffled within each person, must sit within three Monte-Carlo standard errors of chance. ', n(G.shuffled_eeg_scorer_check.cells_within_3_se), ' of ', n(G.shuffled_eeg_scorer_check.cells), ' cells did (', n(G.shuffled_eeg_scorer_check.ssvep_cells), ' SSVEP, ', n(G.shuffled_eeg_scorer_check.boas_cells), ' BOAS).'],
      ['Fit check, on the first fold’s training rows: every conditioned SSVEP arm trained more than 5 pp below the one-output-per-question head, so the declared fallback of ', n(fit['ssvep/L0'].training_epochs), ' epochs applies to every SSVEP arm; sleep, EESM19 and motor imagery stay at ', n(fit['sleep/L1'].training_epochs), '. No fit failed.'],
